    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d847">

                <pb facs="0919" n="909" xml:id="pg909"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">195.91/2–1449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-14T17:00:00+08:00">February 14,
                            1949—5 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 14—5:45 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>230. ReDeptel 76, February 12.<anchor n="87" xml:id="d847-f1"/> Peiping
                    representative Bryner and co-acting as agent APL SS <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >President Fillmore</hi> informed today permission granted unloading vessel
                    Tangku and arrangements completed. He reported also he had accordingly informed
                    APL Shanghai by telegram.</p>
                <p>Repeated Shanghai 188, Nanking 183.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
